<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! engine.checkout.tends ~ the the checkout tunnel converges, each write a ledger generation

`lares repo tend` reads first, then writes only the items that drift (and, with `--force`, the foreign ones, the ledger keeping the bytes it replaced), under the host lock and the radius lock; each tend that writes records one ledger generation `undo` restores. The repo door writes the checkout alone; the radius never widens to the operator's homes.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ tend · force

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`tend` params=`~ converge the checkout's tunnel`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`force` params=`force/true ~ take foreign targets too`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

